{"id":"p1x2","name":"Clean order amounts","lang":"pyspark","entry":"solve","params":["spark","orders_df"],"limit_s":30,"ordered":false,"desc":"<p>An e-commerce site exports its orders as text. <code>orders_df</code> has three string columns:</p>\n<ul><li><code>order_id</code> - the ID of the order;</li><li><code>status</code> - for example <code>\"PAID\"</code>, <code>\" shipped \"</code>, <code>\"Cancelled\"</code>;</li><li><code>amount</code> - the amount typed by sellers: <code>\"45.50\"</code>, <code>\"30,00\"</code>, <code>\" 12 MAD\"</code>, <code>\"\"</code>, <code>\"n/a\"</code> or null.</li></ul>\n<p>Your task is to return the orders whose status is <code>paid</code> or <code>shipped</code>, with the columns <code>order_id</code>, <code>status</code> and <code>amount</code>, where:</p>\n<ol><li><code>status</code> is trimmed and lower-cased;</li><li><code>amount</code> is a double: remove surrounding spaces and the suffix <code>MAD</code> (any case), replace a decimal comma by a dot, then convert;</li><li>an amount that still cannot be converted (empty, text, null) becomes <code>0.0</code>.</li></ol>\n<p>Row order does not matter.</p>\n<h4>Example</h4><p><code>orders_df</code>:</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>status</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>PAID</td><td>45.50</td></tr><tr><td>O2</td><td> shipped </td><td>30,00</td></tr><tr><td>O3</td><td>Cancelled</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>O4</td><td>paid</td><td> 12 MAD</td></tr><tr><td>O5</td><td>Paid</td><td>n/a</td></tr></table></div><p>the output should be</p><div class=\"tblw\"><table><tr><th>order_id</th><th>status</th><th>amount</th></tr><tr><td>O1</td><td>paid</td><td>45.5</td></tr><tr><td>O2</td><td>shipped</td><td>30.0</td></tr><tr><td>O4</td><td>paid</td><td>12.0</td></tr><tr><td>O5</td><td>paid</td><td>0.0</td></tr></table></div>\n<p><b>Note:</b> with Spark 4, <code>.cast(\"double\")</code> on a text like <code>\"n/a\"</code> raises an error. Use <code>try_cast</code>, which returns null instead.</p><div class=\"lim\"><b>[execution time limit]</b> 30 seconds (pyspark)<br><b>[memory limit]</b> 2 GB</div>","starter":"from pyspark.sql import SparkSession, DataFrame, functions as F\n\n\ndef solve(spark: SparkSession, orders_df: DataFrame) -> DataFrame:\n    # write your code here\n    return orders_df\n","hints":["Fais le nettoyage en étapes : trim, puis regexp_replace pour enlever MAD, puis regexp_replace(',', '.').","F.expr(\"try_cast(col AS DOUBLE)\") renvoie null si ce n'est pas un nombre. F.coalesce(x, F.lit(0.0)) remplace le null par 0."],"summary_fr":"Les montants sont du texte sale (virgule décimale, espaces, MAD, vide, texte). Transforme-les en nombre, 0 si illisible. Status en minuscules sans espaces. Garde seulement les commandes dont le status est paid ou shipped.","tags":["nettoyage","regexp_replace","try_cast","lower / trim"],"minutes":15,"source":"Kata Lab","files":null,"visible":[{"input":{"orders_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"order_id STRING, status STRING, amount STRING","rows":[["O1","PAID","45.50"],["O2"," shipped ","30,00"],["O3","Cancelled","12"],["O4","paid"," 12 MAD"],["O5","Paid","n/a"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["order_id","status","amount"],"rows":[["O1","paid",45.5],["O2","shipped",30.0],["O4","paid",12.0],["O5","paid",0.0]]}},{"input":{"orders_df":{"__df__":{"schema":"order_id STRING, status STRING, amount STRING","rows":[["O6","shipped",""],["O7","paid",null],["O8","refunded","5"],["O9"," PAID","7mad"]]}}},"expected":{"columns":["order_id","status","amount"],"rows":[["O6","shipped",0.0],["O7","paid",0.0],["O9","paid",7.0]]}}],"hidden_n":5,"hidden":"","solution":""}